WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
Open Signal Atlas and choose Start setup. This is the running Windows

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.440
app, captured on September twenty ninth. The setup guide leads through browser

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.600
access, a local AI model, topics, and schedules.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:18.770
For live discovery, install the DokoBot command line tool and Edge bridge,

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:23.010
approve the extension, then check the connection. You can also begin with

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:26.130
Discover links only while configuring the rest.

00:00:26.512 --> 00:00:31.792
In Setup, open AI model. LM Studio is the local option and needs

00:00:31.952 --> 00:00:36.992
no OpenAI API key. Install a model in LM Studio, then

00:00:37.072 --> 00:00:39.312
click Find installed models.

00:00:39.682 --> 00:00:44.522
Highlight a model in the installed list and click Use selected model. The

00:00:44.562 --> 00:00:49.282
chosen model appears above the test. Testing the highlighted row saves that

00:00:49.362 --> 00:00:50.962
selection automatically.

00:00:51.348 --> 00:00:56.388
Here, the installed Qwen three four B model loaded in LM Studio,

00:00:56.468 --> 00:01:01.508
analyzed a short diagnostic document, and unloaded successfully. The status

00:01:01.588 --> 00:01:06.708
bar shows the real passing result. If resources are insufficient, the app now

00:01:06.788 --> 00:01:08.708
names the specific constraint.

00:01:09.098 --> 00:01:13.978
Next, configure topics and sources. Topics control what the app looks

00:01:14.058 --> 00:01:18.778
for; sources determine where it searches. The example topics can get you

00:01:19.018 --> 00:01:21.418
started, and you can edit or replace them.

00:01:21.807 --> 00:01:26.927
On Reports, choose cards, a research report, or both. Reports can

00:01:27.007 --> 00:01:31.807
target one to twenty pages, with a research question, audience, and evidence

00:01:32.007 --> 00:01:36.927
supported items such as comparisons, timelines, risk registers, and action

00:01:37.007 --> 00:01:37.807
plans.

00:01:38.182 --> 00:01:43.462
On Home, choose Run Now for the full research pipeline. Discover links

00:01:43.622 --> 00:01:48.902
only creates source cards without AI. After a full run, open Reports to

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:53.622
inspect the cards, narrative HTML, and paginated PDF.

00:01:53.992 --> 00:01:58.392
This is a card digest from a completed public source run. It gives a quick

00:01:58.472 --> 00:02:02.952
view of discovered items and links to their originals. The published example

00:02:03.112 --> 00:02:08.392
used Codex with ChatGPT for analysis; the local LM Studio test shown

00:02:08.472 --> 00:02:10.952
earlier is a separate verified run.

00:02:11.325 --> 00:02:16.525
The same completed example also produced a cited four page report. It includes

00:02:16.565 --> 00:02:21.245
a research question, executive summary, evidence limits, findings, and

00:02:21.325 --> 00:02:26.525
references. The repository provides this PDF and the card digest so you

00:02:26.605 --> 00:02:28.765
can inspect the actual outputs.

00:02:29.135 --> 00:02:33.335
Use your own topics and sources, choose your preferred output, and run a

00:02:33.375 --> 00:02:38.575
manual scan before enabling the schedule. With LM Studio, no OpenAI

00:02:38.655 --> 00:02:43.135
key is needed. Report depth and length depend on the evidence and the model

00:02:43.215 --> 00:02:44.095
you select.
